# Bigint subtraction of large values

Subtracts the smaller 30-digit value from the larger one to verify
arbitrary precision subtraction far beyond 64 bits, producing the full
positive difference 864197532086419753208641975320 without any overflow
limit.

>>> source
first: bigint = 123456789012345678901234567890
second: bigint = 987654321098765432109876543210

// Verifies subtraction reaching a very large positive difference.
difference: bigint = second - first
print(difference)

<<< stdout
864197532086419753208641975320

<<< stderr
